<title>USA: TABLE- American Financial Q2 net drops.</title>
<headline>TABLE- American Financial Q2 net drops.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended June 30</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.26		    $0.41</p>
<p> Shr			   0.26		     0.34</p>
<p> Net			  3,446		    4,473</p>
<p> Revs			 5,121		    8,144</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,357		   13,291</p>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.51		    $0.91</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.51		     0.78</p>
<p> Net			  6,779		   10,370</p>
<p> Revs			10,067		   18,111</p>
<p> Avg			 13,324		   13,291</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers</p>
<p>NOTE: American Financial Enterprises Inc said 1997 earnings would have been comparable to 1996 earnings if it had continued to account for its investment in American Financial Group. The company said it agreed to exchange all its shares of American Financial Group on a one-for-one basis, or $37.00 in cash.</p>
</text>
